## Gradle
.gradle/
build/
app/build/
out/

## Kotlin's own local incremental-compile cache (separate from build/,
## introduced by newer Kotlin Gradle plugin versions) — a real, local-
## only build artifact, not something any commit should ever carry.
.kotlin/

## Local configuration
local.properties

## Android Studio / IntelliJ
.idea/
*.iml

## Claude Code local session/tool-permission state (machine-specific)
.claude/

## Real exported debug logs collected from test devices during live
## diagnostics — contains real peer identity hashes/LXMF addresses/RSSI
## data from actual nearby strangers' devices, never something a commit
## should carry.
debug_logs/
.navigation/
captures/
.externalNativeBuild/
.cxx/

## Chaquopy
app/.python-version
*.whl
app/src/main/python/**/__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

## python-core local test venv artifacts (e.g. `pip install -e .`)
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

## Keystores — never commit *release* signing material
*.jks
*.keystore
## Deliberate, documented exception: debug.keystore (repo root) is a
## real, dedicated debug-signing key, committed on purpose so every
## build — CI or local, any machine — shares one identical debug
## certificate and updates actually work between builds (see
## app/build.gradle.kts's own signingConfigs.debug doc comment for the
## real on-device update failure this fixes). A debug key has none of
## a release key's real security properties — Android itself refuses
## to accept a debug-signed APK as a genuine release build no matter
## what, so there's nothing sensitive being exposed here the way a
## real release keystore would be.
!debug.keystore

## OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

## Logs
*.log
